    "copper mountain": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Copper Mountain",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-12 05:00:00",
      "note": "Good morning and Happy Sunday, everybody! Today we expect to see mostly sunny skies and temps hovering in the mid 40s at mid-mountain elevations. Base areas will be warmer in the low 50s throughout most of the day. WSW winds will be breezy at 15-25mph with gusts into the 40s at times during the afternoon hours. Overnight into tomorrow we expect to see moody, spring weather return bringing a chance of snow flurries each of the next few days. Today is the last day to enjoy some of our terrain on the western half of the resort. It'll be the last hurrah for Timberline Express, Sierra, Rendezvous and Woodward Express. Additionally, today marks the last chance for laps on Storm King and down in Green Acres. Don't worry, we'll be hanging on to the American Flyer, including Central Park, for a bit longer as well as the Eagle, Super Bee and Excelerator lifts. For the latest and greatest terrain and lift info, continue to tune into the Terrain Update channel on Instagram and of course here on coppercolorado.com. Have a great day!",
